#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:337
msgid "Use MPEG-2 hardware acceleration when available"
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:339
msgid ""
"Decode MPEG-2 streams on the GPU (the AppleVA pipeline of Apple's DVD "
"Player) whenever a hardware decoder is present (ATI, Intel GMA950, nVidia), "
"falling back to the libmpeg2 software decoder automatically. Cuts CPU load "
"dramatically on old Macs."
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:343
msgid "Field mode of the MPEG-2 hardware decoder (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:345
msgid ""
"Hardware decoding of field-predicted macroblocks (interlaced streams, DVD). "
"0 = off (interlaced content falls back to the processor); 4 = equivalent "
"frame prediction (the default: the field engine of the GPU tears on motion); "
"1/2/3 = native field engine, for debugging only."
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:349
msgid "Subtitles and OSD over hardware-accelerated video"
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:351
msgid ""
"Compose the subtitles (DVD SPU) and the on-screen display over the picture "
"decoded by the GPU. Without this option the hardware output covers "
"everything and subtitles stay invisible. Only affects the video shown in the "
"VLC window."
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:355
msgid "Asynchronous GPU submission (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:357
msgid ""
"Issue the DVDDriverDecode call on a dedicated thread, so that the VLD of the "
"next picture runs while the GPU works. Measured on the iBook G3: Decode is "
"time spent blocked in the driver, and overlapping it removes the shortfall "
"in the 40 ms per picture budget."
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:361
msgid "10.2 port changes on the hardware path (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:363
msgid ""
"-1 = automatic (on under Mac OS X 10.2 and 10.3, off from 10.4 on, where "
"they replaced behaviour validated on the machine itself), 0 = off, 1 = on."
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:366
msgid "DVD subtitles drawn by the GPU"
msgstr ""

#: modules/codec/libmpeg2.c:368
msgid ""
"Hand the DVD subtitles to the subpicture plane of the ATI hardware decoder: "
"the GPU composes them onto the picture itself, at no per-picture cost, where "
"drawing them through a window costs 15 to 50 ms on this hardware. No effect "
"while hardware decoding is off, as software rendering then takes over."
msgstr ""

